---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Command from '../../components/Command.astro';
import { base, install, latest } from '../../data/site.mjs';

const steps = [['requirements', 'Requirements'], ['install', 'Install mobd'], ['config', 'Configure agents'], ['permissions', 'Grant permissions'], ['run', 'Start mobd'], ['connect', 'Pair a device']];
const more = [['remote', 'Remote access'], ['upgrade', 'Upgrade & uninstall'], ['commands', 'Command reference'], ['faq', 'FAQ']];
const mobd = latest('mobd');
const commands = [
  ['mobd init', 'Create ~/.mobd/config.json; never overwrites an existing file'],
  ['mobd start / stop / restart', 'Start, stop, or reload the configuration'],
  ['mobd start --login', 'Start, and start again at every login'],
  ['mobd status', 'Listening address and readiness checks'],
  ['mobd logs', 'Follow the log (Ctrl-C to stop)'],
  ['mobd serve', 'Run in the foreground'],
  ['mobd link', 'Print a one-time pairing link and QR code for the remote address, else the office network one'],
  ['mobd link --lan', 'The same, always for the office network address'],
  ['mobd link --url URL', 'The same, for exactly this address'],
  ['mobd link --close', 'Cancel invitations that were not used yet'],
  ['mobd remote', 'Show remote access and check it reaches mobd'],
  ['mobd remote setup', 'Set up Tailscale Serve or a Cloudflare Tunnel'],
  ['mobd remote off', 'Turn remote access off; paired devices stay paired'],
  ['mobd clients list', 'List paired devices'],
  ['mobd clients revoke ID', 'Revoke a device and disconnect it now'],
  ['mobd connections', 'List active authenticated requests and streams'],
  ['mobd auth reset --yes', 'Revoke every device and invitation'],
  ['mobd uninstall', 'Stop mobd and remove its service; keeps settings and data'],
];
---
<Layout title="Get started · Mob" description="Install mobd on your office computer, configure Codex or Claude Code, and pair your devices with Mob." readout={{ turn: 'Docs', time: '', place: 'Get started' }}>
  <div class="container-x grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 pt-28 lg:grid-cols-[220px_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:pt-36">
    <details data-mobile-toc class="fold sticky top-[72px] z-30 rounded-xl bg-[#0b0b0f]/95 backdrop-blur lg:hidden">
      <summary>Contents</summary>
      <nav aria-label="Guide (mobile)" class="grid gap-1 pb-3 text-sm">
        {[...steps, ...more].map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`} class="py-1 text-zinc-300">{label}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </details>

    <aside class="hidden lg:block">
      <nav data-doc-nav aria-label="Guide" class="sticky top-32 text-sm">
        <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500">Quick start</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-0.5">
          {steps.map(([id, label], i) => <a href={`#${id}`} class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 data-[active]:bg-white/[0.06] data-[active]:text-zinc-50"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-400">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{label}</a>)}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500">More</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-0.5">
          {more.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`} class="rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 data-[active]:bg-white/[0.06] data-[active]:text-zinc-50">{label}</a>)}
        </div>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="doc max-w-3xl">
      <header class="mb-14">
        <p class="eyebrow">Docs</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl">Get started</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-400">About ten minutes: prepare the office computer, then pair your first device.{mobd && <> This guide matches mobd <span class="font-mono text-zinc-200">{mobd.version}</span>.</>}</p>
      </header>

      <section id="requirements">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">01</span>Requirements</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>An office Mac with <strong>Apple Silicon</strong> and <strong>macOS 13</strong> or later that stays on, online and logged in. mobd for Linux and Windows is coming.</li>
          <li><a href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/" rel="noreferrer">Codex CLI</a> or <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/quickstart" rel="noreferrer">Claude Code</a> installed and signed in on it. More agent harnesses are coming.</li>
          <li>Your devices can reach that Mac: the same LAN, a company VPN, or <a href="/remote/">remote access</a> (Tailscale or a Cloudflare Tunnel).</li>
          <li>A client: <a href="/download/#mac">Mob for macOS</a>, <a href="/download/#ios">iPhone and iPad (iOS 17+)</a> or <a href="/download/#android">Android 8.0+</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="install">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">02</span>Install mobd</h2>
        <p>In Terminal on the office Mac, as your normal user (no sudo):</p>
        <Command command={install} />
        <p>The installer checks the SHA-256 and the Apple developer signature and puts only <code>mobd</code> in <code>~/.local/bin</code>. Add that to your PATH and check:</p>
        <pre>echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' &gt;&gt; ~/.zshrc
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
mobd --version</pre>
        <details class="fold"><summary>A specific version, another directory, or a manual install</summary>
          <pre>curl -fsSLO {base}/mobd/install.sh
sh install.sh --version X.Y.Z
sh install.sh --install-dir /absolute/path</pre>
          <p>Or download the archive from the <a href="/download/#mobd">download page</a>, check it against SHA256SUMS, unpack it and put <code>mobd</code> in a directory on your PATH.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section id="config">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">03</span>Configure agents</h2>
        <pre>mobd init      # creates ~/.mobd/config.json, never overwrites
open -e ~/.mobd/config.json</pre>
        <div data-tabs class="my-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08]">
          <div role="tablist" class="flex border-b border-white/[0.08] bg-white/[0.03] text-sm">
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-codex" aria-controls="cfg-codex" aria-selected="true" class="px-4 py-2 text-zinc-400 aria-selected:border-b-2 aria-selected:border-accent-400 aria-selected:text-zinc-50">Codex</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-claude" aria-controls="cfg-claude" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="px-4 py-2 text-zinc-400 aria-selected:border-b-2 aria-selected:border-accent-400 aria-selected:text-zinc-50">Claude Code</button>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="cfg-codex" aria-labelledby="tab-codex"><pre class="!my-0 !rounded-none !border-0">{`{
  "listen": "0.0.0.0:8080",
  "workdir": "/Users/you/Projects",
  "codexBin": "codex",
  "runners": ["codex"],
  "defaultRunner": "codex",
  "codexPermissions": "approve"
}`}</pre></div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="cfg-claude" aria-labelledby="tab-claude" hidden><pre class="!my-0 !rounded-none !border-0">{`{
  "listen": "0.0.0.0:8080",
  "workdir": "/Users/you/Projects",
  "claudeBin": "claude",
  "runners": ["claude"],
  "defaultRunner": "claude",
  "claudePermissions": "approve"
}`}</pre></div>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><code>codexBin</code> / <code>claudeBin</code>: a command name is enough when it is on your PATH; otherwise find the full path with <code>command -v codex</code>.</li>
          <li><code>"approve"</code>: the agent asks you before commands and file edits. Without it the default is <code>"bypass"</code>, which never asks.</li>
          <li><code>listen</code> defaults to <code>0.0.0.0:8080</code> so devices on your LAN and VPN can connect. With Tailscale only, use <code>127.0.0.1:8080</code>.</li>
          <li>JSON does not expand <code>~</code> or <code>$HOME</code>; write full paths. Run <code>mobd restart</code> after a change.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="callout"><strong>Open it on trusted networks only.</strong> Every device must pair, but plain HTTP is not encrypted. Never forward port 8080 to the internet; across networks see <a href="/remote/">Remote access</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="permissions">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">04</span>Grant permissions</h2>
        <p>mobd asks for missing permissions the first time it starts. You can also grant them in <strong>System Settings → Privacy & Security</strong>.</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Permission</th><th scope="col">Used for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Screen & System Audio Recording</td><td>Screenshots and the live view</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Accessibility</td><td>Controlling the mouse and keyboard from your device</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>
        <p>mobd captures the screen itself; Screen Sharing does not need to be on. Keep the office Mac from sleeping while nobody is at it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="run">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">05</span>Start mobd</h2>
        <pre>mobd start                        # run in the background
mobd status                       # address and readiness checks
mobd stop && mobd start --login   # optional: also start at login</pre>
        <p>Every check in <code>mobd status</code> should pass. <code>mobd logs</code> follows the log.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="connect">
        <h2><span class="mr-3 font-mono text-accent-400">06</span>Pair a device</h2>
        <p>Each device pairs once. Its credential is kept in the Keychain or Android Keystore and it reconnects on its own afterwards. On the office Mac, create an invitation:</p>
        <pre>mobd link</pre>
        <p>Terminal shows the address it used (this Mac's office network address, or the <a href="/remote/">remote address</a> once set up), a QR code and a link, <strong>valid for 10 minutes and for one use</strong>. Run <code>mobd link</code> again if it expires. With mobd 0.2.0, name the address: <code>mobd link --url http://192.168.1.100:8080</code>.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>In Mob, open <strong>Settings → Machines → Add machine</strong>.</li>
          <li>Scan the QR code with your phone, or paste the whole link. Check the address and tap <strong>Pair</strong>.</li>
          <li>Start a conversation and try something simple, such as “Look at the screen and tell me what you see.”</li>
        </ol>
        <p><code>mobd clients list</code> shows paired devices. If one is lost, <code>mobd clients revoke CLIENT_ID</code> disconnects it immediately.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="remote">
        <h2>Remote access</h2>
        <p>Away from the office network, reach mobd through <strong>Tailscale Serve</strong> (private, your devices run the Tailscale app) or a <strong id="cloudflare">Cloudflare Tunnel</strong> (no app on the phone, needs your domain). <code>mobd remote setup</code> walks you through either, checks the address reaches mobd and makes <code>mobd link</code> use it.</p>
        <p><a href="/remote/" class="btn-ghost">Remote access guide</a></p>
        <p>The guide compares the methods and covers the manual steps, Tailscale Funnel, using the same Mac at the office and away, security, and problems.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="upgrade">
        <h2>Upgrade & uninstall</h2>
        <p><strong>Upgrade mobd:</strong> let running tasks finish, run <code>mobd stop</code>, run the <a href="#install">install command</a> again, then <code>mobd start</code>. Settings and conversations are kept.</p>
        <p><strong>Upgrade the apps:</strong> the macOS app updates itself; on Android install the new APK over the old one; iPhone and iPad update through the App Store.</p>
        <p><strong>Uninstall mobd:</strong> run <code>mobd uninstall</code>, then delete <code>~/.local/bin/mobd</code>. Settings live in <code>~/.mobd</code> and conversations in <code>~/Library/Application Support/mob</code>; delete them if you no longer need them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="commands">
        <h2>Command reference</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{commands.map(([c, d]) => <tr><td class="whitespace-nowrap"><code>{c}</code></td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table></div>
        <p>Every setting is listed in the <a href="https://github.com/xrdavies/mobd#configuration-reference" rel="noreferrer">mobd configuration reference</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <details class="fold"><summary>Does the office Mac have to stay on?</summary><p>Yes. mobd and the agents run on it; while it sleeps or is off, devices can't connect and tasks pause.</p></details>
        <details class="fold"><summary>Is my data uploaded anywhere?</summary><p>Mob runs no server of its own: your devices connect to mobd directly, or through the remote-access service you choose (Tailscale, Cloudflare). Whether task content goes to a model service depends on the agent and model you use. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p></details>
        <details class="fold"><summary>Mob says the machine needs pairing</summary><p>This device's credential was revoked, or the office reset authentication. Run <code>mobd link --url …</code> again, choose <strong>Pair again</strong> in Mob and scan or paste the new link. Conversations are kept.</p></details>
        <details class="fold"><summary>I can chat, but there is no live view</summary><p>Mob shows the reason. Without Screen Recording permission, grant it and restart mobd; if it says “Update mobd”, upgrade the office computer.</p></details>
        <details class="fold"><summary>Intel Macs, Linux, Windows?</summary><p>mobd and the macOS app currently need Apple Silicon and macOS 13 or later. mobd for Linux and Windows, and Mob for Windows and Linux, are on the way.</p></details>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
